                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Especially considering the price, this is a very simple game that becomes tiresome quickly.  It's sort of the ship-sailing part of Pillars of Eternity 2 but with more detailed ship battles and without any island exploration.  There's a very basic story.\n\nThe main focus is on fighting things in the ship fighting mode and upgrading your ship (when you can find an open port).  The fights are basic and involve moving your crew to different stations and waiting for cannons to fire, leaks to repair, etc.  Once you've fought 2 or 3 ships/enemies (no spoilers..), you've essentially fought them all.\n\nI can't recommend this game at the current price.  At $10 or so I'd say it's a fun enough distraction for a few hours, if you really like the idea of the ship fighting mode where you face off against an enemy and fire things at them while repairing your ship, healing your crew, etc.  But really, I can't recommend this game for the general gaming populace.  It's too simple and there isn't much happening.",
